meta {
  name: Refresh Token
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/auth/refresh
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "refresh_token": "{{refresh_token}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200 && res.getBody().refresh_token) {
    bru.setEnvVar("refresh_token", res.getBody().refresh_token);
  }
}

docs {
  Tokens rotate: the response carries a **new** `refresh_token` and the one you presented is
  revoked. The post-response script stores the new one automatically.

  Presenting a token that was already exchanged is treated as a leak, not a mistake — the
  whole session is revoked and you get a 401. Try it twice with the same token to see it.
}
